      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not a new patch, we\u0027ve carried 056f12819b75 (\"ANDROID: arm64: copy CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND from ARM\") since 2014. The issue is that a very similar patch landed upstream: 1e40d105dae5 (\"arm64: Extend the kernel command line from the bootloader\") which also added CMDLINE_EXTEND for arm64. We even had merge conflicts with it: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/1530042/3/arch/arm64/Kconfig.\n\nWill\u0027s removal of CMDLINE_EXTEND in cae118b6acc3 (\"arm64: Drop support for CMDLINE_EXTEND\") was only targeting upstream and not android (See b/120440972#comment12). However, by pulling this from upstream we also broke the android patch.\n\nI could help out get the new approach upstream (append and prepend). In the meantime we need to restore CMDLINE_EXTEND on arm64 for android. Otherwise this decade old patch becomes useless for arm64: d9a2a3f2c2c4 (\"ANDROID: of: Support CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND config option\").",
